# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Beyond: properties
d.sec('4.z-properties-of-determinants')
b('Effect of transposing: |Aᵀ| = ?', T('|Aᵀ| = |A|') + '. So anything true for rows is true for columns')
b('What happens to |A| if two rows (or columns) are interchanged?', 'It ' + T('changes sign') + '. So an even number of swaps leaves it unchanged')
b('What if two rows (or columns) are identical or proportional?', T('|A| = 0') + ' (swapping the equal rows must change the sign but does not change the matrix, so |A| = −|A|)')
b('What if a row is multiplied by k?', T('|A|') + ' is multiplied by k. So a common factor of a row can be taken outside; for the whole matrix |kA| = kⁿ|A|')
b('Which row operation does not change the determinant?', T('Rᵢ → Rᵢ + kRⱼ') + ' (add a multiple of another row); same for columns. Use it to create zeros before expanding')
b('If every element of a row is a sum of two terms, what can you do?', 'Split into a sum of two determinants (the other rows unchanged): |a+p, b+q; c, d| = |a b; c d| + |p q; c d|')
b('Trap: is |A + B| = |A| + |B|?', X('No') + '. The determinant is not additive. It is multiplicative: |AB| = |A||B|. Only the “one row is a sum” splitting works')
b('How do row operations help evaluate a determinant quickly? Example: |1 2 3; 4 5 6; 7 8 9|.', 'R₂ − R₁ = (3, 3, 3) and R₃ − R₂ = (3, 3, 3): two equal rows, so ' + N('0'))
b('Determinant of a skew-symmetric matrix of odd order?', N('0') + '. |A| = |Aᵀ| = |−A| = (−1)ⁿ|A| = −|A| for odd n')
b('If A is n × n with A² = I, what are the possible values of |A|?', '|A|² = 1 so ' + N('|A| = ±1') + '. Same if AAᵀ = I (orthogonal)')
b('If A is 3 × 3 with |A| = 2, find |3A|, |adj A|, |A⁻¹|, |A²|, |Aᵀ|.', '|3A| = 27 · 2 = ' + N('54') + '; |adj A| = |A|² = ' + N('4') + '; |A⁻¹| = ' + N('1/2') + '; |A²| = ' + N('4') + '; |Aᵀ| = ' + N('2'))
b('If A is 3 × 3, |A| = 4, find |adj(adj A)|.', '|adj A| = |A|² = 16 and |adj(adj A)| = 16² = ' + N('256 = |A|⁴') + ' (general: |adj(adj A)| = |A|^((n−1)²))')
b('Vandermonde determinant |1 a a²; 1 b b²; 1 c c²| = ?', N('(b − a)(c − a)(c − b)') + '. It vanishes iff two of a, b, c are equal. Ex 4.3 Q4 is the similar (x − y)(y − z)(z − x)')
b('Circulant/symmetric trick: |a b c; b c a; c a b| = ?', N('−(a³ + b³ + c³ − 3abc)') + ' = −(a + b + c)(a² + b² + c² − ab − bc − ca)')
b('Determinant of a triangular 4 × 4 matrix with diagonal 1, 2, 3, 4?', 'Product of the diagonal entries: ' + N('24'))
b('For which k is [[k, 2], [3, k + 1]] singular?', 'k(k + 1) − 6 = 0 → k² + k − 6 = 0 → ' + N('k = 2 or −3'))
b('Solve |x + 1, 3; 5, x + 3| = 0.', '(x + 1)(x + 3) − 15 = x² + 4x − 12 = 0 → ' + N('x = 2 or x = −6'))
b('For which λ does x + y + z = 0, x + 2y + 3z = 0, 2x + 3y + λz = 0 have non-trivial solutions?', 'Determinant |1 1 1; 1 2 3; 2 3 λ| = (2λ − 9) − (λ − 6) + (3 − 4) = λ − 4 = 0 → ' + N('λ = 4'))
b('Area of the triangle with vertices (0, 0), (a, 0), (0, b) using the determinant?', '½ |0 0 1; a 0 1; 0 b 1| = ½ · |ab| = ' + N('ab/2'))

